    "runtime_evidence": "vLLM 0.21.0 image labels identify build commit ad7125a431e176d4161099480a66f0169609a690. Image config inspection showed Entrypoint [\"vllm\", \"serve\"] and image env VLLM_ENABLE_CUDA_COMPATIBILITY=0. A 2026-05-23T03Z B300 diagnostic pod with the same regional image showed NVIDIA B300 SXM6 AC, ptxas release 13.0 V13.0.88, torch 2.11.0+cu130, CUDA 13.0, device capability (10, 3), triton 3.6.0, vLLM 0.21.0, and a successful BF16 CUDA matmul. 2026-05-23T04Z retained probes proved the manifest must not pass duplicate `serve` or `--model` args; it now uses the image's built-in vLLM serve entrypoint with only the positional model id and leaves the image default CUDA compatibility mode in place. The final 2026-05-23T04Z B300 probe reached vLLM serving, selected FlashInfer/TRTLLM attention, loaded SmolLM3ForCausalLM, returned HTTP 200, and completed 10 measured warm requests. The 2026-05-23T12Z remaining-cell probe used the same digest and manifest args and completed 10 measured warm requests on B200, H200, L40S, and RTX6000.",
